Historically, we have financed our liquidity requirements through cash generated from our operations. Net cash provided by operating activities during the nine months ended March 31, 2025 was $2.92 billion compared to $2.42 billion during the nine months ended March 31, 2024. This increase of $501.0 million resulted primarily from the following:

• An increase in customer and other collections of approximately $760 million primarily driven by higher shipments;

• An increase in interest income of approximately $26 million from higher cash balances and higher interest rates; and

• A decrease in income tax payments of approximately $109 million as we paid off the delayed tax payments from prior fiscal year in October 2023 as a result of the California Flood Tax Relief; partially offset by

• An increase in accounts payable payments of approximately $270 million;

• An increase in employee-related payments of approximately $80 million;
